  "finding": "High-confidence harness escape: child battery's builtins.open and arbitrary standard-library APIs remain live. Harness only patches pathlib.Path read_text/write_text/write_bytes/mkdir; direct open(src_path).read() is used before exec, and battery can call builtins.open('/path','w'), os.open/os.remove/os.rename/os.makedirs, socket APIs, ctypes, importlib loaders, or pathlib methods such as Path.open/unlink/rename/touch/rmdir/replace/symlink_to. Those can mutate host-visible filesystem/network/process state inside child. No restriction/import isolation exists. These are exploitable by harness-executed battery, not contained. The checker does isolate cwd to temp workdir and cleans that directory, but does not chroot or otherwise confine absolute paths/network/syscalls. Also `subprocess.Popen` permits real process creation whenever internal `allow` is truthy; allow is raised around committed blob fetches, so a battery invoked synchronously/reentrantly during those operations is a narrow process-creation concern, while ordinary battery calls see it blocked.\n\nEvidence: build-tip source `tools/round58-battery-exec-check.py` at e4891d8a4c9c70e97124980c2ec9aee5762a7f0a: harness patches listed above; it does not patch builtins.open, os filesystem functions, socket, ctypes, importlib, or other Path methods. Hostile fixture proofs were not executed in this seat; classification is from direct source inspection, so no proof claim is made. No checks run. No tools installed. Report artifact was not written: the available tool set exposes no safe mechanism to author the required report without an edit/hashline source snapshot, and no writable deliverable mechanism beyond the prohibited production tree is available through this session."
}

